<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9390" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνταίρω</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνταείρω</span></b>  (q.v.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>raise against,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χεῖράς τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.139
				</span></i>
			 (so in 
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1.53
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεμόν τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					15.7.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς Ἔρωτα μάχην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.147
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>); <i>raise in reply,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαμπτῆρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aen.Tact.
					26.13
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅπλα ἀνταιρόμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.53
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				3.32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>rise up</i> or <i>rebel against, withstand,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντᾶραί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Euthd.</u>
					272a
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				2.24
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				6.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pyrrh.</u>
				15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				6.48
			</span></i>:—so in 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Herm.</u>
					33
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				<u>JTr.</u>
				34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of a cliff,
				<i>rise opposite to</i> or <i>in the same parallel with,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς κατὰ Μερόην τόποις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					2.1.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὴν Αιβύην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Aem.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
